{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'rg -n \"AI_POLICY|Pull Request|pull request|issue first|collaborator\" CONTRIBUTING.md AI_POLICY.md'","aggregated_output":"AI_POLICY.md:1:This project accepts AI generated Pull Requests, as long as the following guidelines are met.\nAI_POLICY.md:3:- The Pull Request must fill in the repository's pull request template.\nAI_POLICY.md:4:- The Pull Request must identify itself as AI generated, including the name of the agent used.\nAI_POLICY.md:5:- The Pull Request must link to a issue or discussion where a solution has been approved by a maintainer (@willmcgugan).\nCONTRIBUTING.md:3:This project welcomes contributions in the form of Pull Requests.\nCONTRIBUTING.md:9:See also [AI_POLICY.md](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/blob/master/AI_POLICY.md) if you will be using AI.\nCONTRIBUTING.md:87:Please add type annotations for all new code, and ensure that type checking succeeds before creating a pull request.\nCONTRIBUTING.md:118:Before submitting your pull request, update the `CHANGELOG.md` file describing, briefly, what you've done.\nCONTRIBUTING.md:132:## Creating A Pull Request\nCONTRIBUTING.md:134:Once you're happy with your change and have ensured that all steps above have been followed (and checks have passed), you can create a pull request.\nCONTRIBUTING.md:136:Please ensure that you include a good description of what your change does in your pull request, and link it to any relevant issues or discussions.\nCONTRIBUTING.md:138:When you create your pull request, we'll run the checks described earlier. If they fail, please attempt to fix them as we're unlikely to be able to review your code until then.\nCONTRIBUTING.md:139:If you've exhausted all options on trying to fix a failing check, feel free to leave a note saying so in the pull request and someone may be able to offer assistance.\nCONTRIBUTING.md:143:After the checks in your pull request pass, someone will review your code.\nCONTRIBUTING.md:148:When the pull request is approved, it will be merged into the `master` branch.\nCONTRIBUTING.md:155:Rich receives a growing number of AI-written issues and pull requests, and new\nCONTRIBUTING.md:168:4. Pull requests follow [AI_POLICY.md](AI_POLICY.md): fill in the template,\nCONTRIBUTING.md:185:  issue or copy the bot's comment into a new issue or pull request.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
